    {
      "note": "The distance expression עַד מֵרָחֹוק is rendered jointly by ‘far off’: עַד sets the extent reached, מִן forms the distal adverb with רָחֹוק, and רָחֹוק supplies the distance lexeme. The competing split assigns ‘off’ to מִן and leaves עַד unrepresented, but ‘off’ here completes the English distance expression rather than independently expressing an ablative ‘from’; that ownership is not clearly preferable to the fused rendering. The lexical heads are רָחֹוק and ‘far’.",
